on memberCanEdit (adrMsgTable, adrMember, adrSite=nil) {
	«News items have diffrent rules about who can edit them. It's not necessarily true that the original author can edit his or her news items -- if it's been released for posting, then you must be a managing editor.
		«Call this script only if you know this is a Manila site and you know adrMsgTable points to a news item in the dg.
		«04/25/00; 2:27:58 PM by PBS
	«Changes:
		«9/8/03; 4:57:16 PM by JES
			«Content editors can edit any news item. This editorial class was missed when the content editor was added to Manila.
				«Quote from the docs: "The Content Editor can edit all the stories, pictures, and messages on a site like a Managing Editor but can't edit templates and set the various site preferences."
				«http://manilanewbies.userland.com/stories/storyReader$6089
		«8/19/01; 11:56:04 PM by JES
			«Modified to make it possibled to call this script from outside the website framework context. All that was required was an additional parameter: adrSite. If nil (the default) then it's assumed that we're in the website framework context. Otherwise, it doesn't matter what the context is.
	
	local (flManagingEditor = false, flContentEditor = false);
	if adrSite == nil { //assume we're called in the website framework context
		local (pta = html.getPageTableAddress ());
		adrSite = manilaSuite.getManilaSiteAddress (pta);
		flManagingEditor = manilaSuite.editors.managingEditorTest (pta);
		flContentEditor = manilaSuite.editors.contentEditorTest (pta)}
	else { //we're called from an RPC handler or some other script
		local (siteName = manilaSuite.getCanonicalSiteName (adrSite));
		local (username = nameOf (adrMember^));
		flManagingEditor = manilaSuite.rpcUtils.isManagingEditor (siteName, username);
		flContentEditor = manilaSuite.rpcUtils.isContentEditor (siteName, username)};
	
	«First check custody.
	bundle {
		if not (manilaSuite.custody.memberCanCheckOutObject (adrMsgTable, adrMember, adrSite, true)) {
			return (false)}};
	
	«local (flManagingEditor = manilaSuite.editors.managingEditorTest (pta)) //8/19/01 JES: commented out; see if adrSite == nil, above.
	if flManagingEditor or flContentEditor { //managing editors and content editors can always edit, no matter what
		return (true)};
	
	if manilaSuite.news.isReleased (adrMsgTable) { //once released, only an ME may edit
		return (false)};
	
	«It's not released, so it can be edited by the member.
	local (flMemberIsAuthor = false, memberKey);
	memberKey = nameOf (adrMember^);
	if string.lower (memberKey) == string.lower (adrMsgTable^.member) {
		flMemberIsAuthor = true};
	if flMemberIsAuthor {
		return (true)};
	
	return (false)}